  "description": "From effortless trips to the store to traffic-free commutes, an e-bike is a great way to bring more smiles to your day. This second generation 407 gets a larger battery for a little more range and uses Shimano’s new Cues drivetrain. Tailor-made for urban adventures, the light and strong aluminum frame pairs well with the efficient Shimano Steps drive unit. There are multiple modes to give your pedalling a little extra oomph; from eco’s subtle ‘wind at your back’ feeling, to the hill-levelling power of high mode. And little touches like high volume tires, a wide seat, ergonomic grips, and front suspension help make gravel roads feel like bike lanes.\n\nAluminum 6061 alloy frame keeps weight low and strength high\n\nLower top tube makes mounting and dismounting easier\n\nShimano Steps E5000 drive unit provides smooth pedalling assistance up to 32km/h\n\nBar mounted computer and controller cycles through modes (off, walk, eco normal and high), turns on lights, and gives information about your bike\n\nComputer is Bluetooth™ and ANT compatible for use with fitness sensors\n\n504WH battery lithium-ion battery provides up to lots of range and is locked in the frame\n\nRemovable battery lets you have more than one battery, great for long days in the saddle\n\nDistance on a charge varies based on ride conditions, things like: assistance level, wind, hills, road surface, frequency of starting and stopping, etc. all impact range, expect somewhere between 25 and 150km\n\nTo keep your battery performing at its best, follow the manufacturer’s guidelines regarding storage and charging conditions (e-Bike batteries can be very sensitive to cold temperatures)\n\nSR Suntour front suspension fork with lockout, smooths out the bumps in the road\n\nShimano MT200 hydraulic disc brakes provide outstanding stopping power in all weather conditions\n\n9-speed Shimano Cues drivetrain provides smooth, reliable shifting, and gearing to compliment the Steps drive unit\n\nThe Cues line provides reliable performance, durability, and easy maintenance – with cross compatibility across the line\n\nIntegrated front and rear lights help you see and be seen\n\nKickstand means you always have a parking spot for your new e-bike\n\nFenders and chain cover help keep you dry on those wet weather commutes\n\nBikes are covered by MEC's Rocksolid Guarantee and Bike Service Agreement. You can bring your bike to any MEC bike shop for free adjustments and minor maintenance for a year after purchase\n\nMEC bikes are designed in Canada. Everything from the frames to the graphics were developed at the MEC Head Office in Vancouver, BC\n\nDue to challenges with supply chain, components may be substituted for comparable parts at any time. The listed build is how MEC intended your bike to arrive, though the manufacturer may need to make a tweak or two to get you riding sooner",
